---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="FileLocker Security — AES-256-GCM Encryption, Argon2id, 100% Offline"
  description="FileLocker uses AES-256-GCM encryption and Argon2id key derivation. All encryption and decryption happens locally on your device — no server, no cloud, no data transmission."
>
  <Navbar currentPath="/security" />

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow center">Security</div>
      <h1>Military-grade is not marketing. It's mathematics.</h1>
      <p>How FileLocker protects your files — and what actually happens during encryption and decryption.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW FILELOCKER PROTECTS -->
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="security-section">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Encryption</div>
          <h2>AES-256-GCM: the same standard used by governments.</h2>
          <p>FileLocker uses AES-256-GCM — the encryption standard approved by the US government for classified information. It is used by banks, governments, and the US military. Without the exact password, the files are completely unreadable — not difficult to read, not expensive to break. Mathematically impossible to open without the correct key.</p>
          <p>GCM (Galois/Counter Mode) adds authentication on top of encryption — meaning that if even a single byte of the locked file is changed or corrupted, decryption fails. This guarantees the integrity of your delivered file.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="badge-grid">
          <div class="sec-badge">AES-256-GCM Encryption</div>
          <div class="sec-badge">Argon2id Key Derivation</div>
          <div class="sec-badge">HIPAA Workflow Support</div>
          <div class="sec-badge">GDPR Article 32</div>
          <div class="sec-badge">Zero Data Transmission</div>
          <div class="sec-badge">100% Offline</div>
          <div class="sec-badge">No Cloud Infrastructure</div>
          <div class="sec-badge">Web Crypto API</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT FILELOCKER DOES (8-STEP ARCHITECTURE) -->
  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head center">
        <div class="eyebrow center">Security Architecture</div>
        <h2>The 8-Step Local Encryption Flow</h2>
        <p>FileLocker operates entirely offline. Below is the exact technical lifecycle of a protected file — explicitly showing what happens on your device versus the recipient's device. <strong>At no point do FileLocker servers receive or process any data.</strong></p>
      </div>
      
      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap:32px;">
        <div style="background:#0F1420; padding:24px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
          <span class="step-num mono">1. File Selection</span>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--color-ink-soft);margin-top:12px;">You select a document or folder on your local Windows machine. The file never leaves your RAM.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#0F1420; padding:24px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
          <span class="step-num mono">2. Local Processing</span>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--color-ink-soft);margin-top:12px;">The FileLocker desktop application reads the file entirely offline. No network requests are made.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#0F1420; padding:24px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
          <span class="step-num mono">3. Key Derivation</span>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--color-ink-soft);margin-top:12px;">Your password is processed locally using Argon2id to derive a secure cryptographic key.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#0F1420; padding:24px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
          <span class="step-num mono">4. AES-256-GCM</span>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--color-ink-soft);margin-top:12px;">The file buffer is encrypted in-memory using AES-256-GCM. The plaintext is then wiped from memory.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#0F1420; padding:24px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
          <span class="step-num mono">5. Vault Generation</span>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--color-ink-soft);margin-top:12px;">A self-contained `.html` file is generated containing the encrypted ciphertext and the unlock interface.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#0F1420; padding:24px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
          <span class="step-num mono">6. Delivery</span>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--color-ink-soft);margin-top:12px;">You deliver the locked file via email or USB. Even if intercepted, it remains mathematically protected.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#0F1420; padding:24px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
          <span class="step-num mono">7. Browser Decryption</span>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--color-ink-soft);margin-top:12px;">The recipient opens the file in a standard browser. Their password derives the key locally via Web Crypto API.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#0F1420; padding:24px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
          <span class="step-num mono">8. File Extraction</span>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--color-ink-soft);margin-top:12px;">The original file is extracted directly to the recipient's local Downloads folder. No servers are involved.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ARGON2ID -->
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Password security</div>
        <h2>Passwords that resist brute force attacks.</h2>
        <p>Your password is not stored as-is. FileLocker transforms it using Argon2id — a system designed to make automated password-guessing attacks computationally impossible, even on modern hardware with dedicated GPUs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="threat-list">
        <div class="threat-row">
          <span class="label">USB drive lost or stolen</span>
          <span class="status protected">Protected</span>
        </div>
        <div class="threat-row">
          <span class="label">File intercepted during email delivery</span>
          <span class="status protected">Protected</span>
        </div>
        <div class="threat-row">
          <span class="label">Brute force password attack</span>
          <span class="status protected">Protected via Argon2id</span>
        </div>
        <div class="threat-row">
          <span class="label">File tampered in transit</span>
          <span class="status protected">Detected via GCM authentication</span>
        </div>
        <div class="threat-row">
          <span class="label">Cloud server breach</span>
          <span class="status protected">Not applicable — no cloud used</span>
        </div>
        <div class="threat-row">
          <span class="label">Password forgotten by sender</span>
          <span class="status by-design">No recovery — by design</span>
        </div>
        <div class="threat-row">
          <span class="label">Password shared insecurely (same channel as file)</span>
          <span class="status by-design">User responsibility</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- COMPLIANCE -->
  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Compliance workflows</div>
        <h2>Designed for professionals handling sensitive data.</h2>
        <p>FileLocker is suitable for professionals handling confidential information who need to demonstrate that documents were delivered with appropriate protection measures.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid" style="max-width:760px;">
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>HIPAA Workflows</h3>
          <p>FileLocker's local encryption and offline operation supports workflows requiring that protected health information (PHI) is transmitted with appropriate safeguards.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>GDPR Article 32</h3>
          <p>GDPR Article 32 requires appropriate technical measures for personal data security. AES-256-GCM encryption and local processing support these requirements.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>ABA Rule 1.6</h3>
          <p>ABA Rule 1.6 requires lawyers to make reasonable efforts to prevent unauthorized disclosure of client information. FileLocker's encrypted delivery supports this obligation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:24px;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--color-ink-faint);">Note: FileLocker supports compliant workflows. It does not constitute legal advice or formal compliance certification. Consult your compliance officer or legal counsel for guidance specific to your situation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="final-cta">
        <h2>Protection that starts before delivery.</h2>
        <p>Request Access and be notified when FileLocker is available.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions" style="justify-content:center;margin-bottom:18px;">
          <a href="/early-access" class="btn btn-primary">Request Access &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/how-it-works" class="btn btn-ghost">See how it works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
